<ansi fg="black-bold">.:</ansi> <ansi fg="magenta">Help for </ansi><ansi fg="command">quests</ansi>

A quest is a task someone in the world asks you to do, like finding a
lost item or chasing off a beast. Most quests have a few steps. You get
a reward when you finish.

<ansi fg="yellow">Finding a quest: </ansi>

  When you look at a room, a mark in front of a person's name tells you
  they have something for you:

  <ansi fg="yellow">[!]</ansi>  they have a new quest for you.
  <ansi fg="yellow">[?]</ansi>  you can finish a quest with them now.
  <ansi fg="yellow">[*]</ansi>  they have something important to tell you, or you can
       report a step of a quest to them.

  To take a quest, type <ansi fg="command">talk</ansi> <ansi fg="cyan"><name></ansi> and choose the <ansi fg="yellow">[!]</ansi> line from
  the numbered list. They tell you what they want. Then choose <ansi fg="yellow">Accept</ansi>
  to take the quest, or <ansi fg="yellow">Leave</ansi> to say no for now.

  To finish a quest, talk to the person marked <ansi fg="yellow">[?]</ansi> and choose the
  <ansi fg="yellow">[?]</ansi> line. Some steps in the middle of a quest work the same way,
  through a line marked <ansi fg="yellow">[*]</ansi>. If the quest asks for an item,
  choosing the line hands it over. See <ansi fg="command">help talk</ansi>.

<ansi fg="yellow">Your quest list: </ansi>

  The <ansi fg="command">quests</ansi> command lists the quests you are working on. Each one
  shows its name, a progress bar, and what to do for your current step.
  Finished quests are hidden. Add <ansi fg="command">all</ansi> to list them too.

<ansi fg="yellow">Quests you can repeat: </ansi>

  Some work can be taken again after a while. The quest list marks it
  <ansi fg="yellow">(repeatable)</ansi>. When you offer to do it again, the person tells you so,
  and some work can only be done a set number of times. Until it is time,
  they do not offer it. Add <ansi fg="command">all</ansi> to the list to see each one you finished:

  <ansi fg="yellow">Ready to take on again</ansi>   talk to the person and take it once more.
  <ansi fg="yellow">Not offered again yet</ansi>    wait a while, then it comes back.
  <ansi fg="yellow">Done for good</ansi>            you have done it as often as it allows.

<ansi fg="yellow">Usage: </ansi>

  <ansi fg="command">quests</ansi>              Show the quests you are working on
  <ansi fg="command">quests all</ansi>          Show every quest you have started, finished ones too

Stuck on a step? <ansi fg="command">hint</ansi> gives a nudge for your current quest, and
<ansi fg="command">hint [name]</ansi> gives one for a quest you name. When you have no quest
in progress, <ansi fg="command">hint</ansi> tells you how to find one.

<ansi fg="magenta-bold">See also:</ansi> <ansi fg="command">help talk</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help hint</ansi>
